<title>UK: ASCOT TO SELL FRENCH UNIT FOR 8.6 MLN STG.</title>
<headline>ASCOT TO SELL FRENCH UNIT FOR 8.6 MLN STG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British diversified industrial and services company Ascot Holdings Plc said it was planning to sell its French subsidiary Clearplas France S.A. for about FFR85 million (8.6 million stg).  </p>
<p>Ascot said it was selling the firm to a unit of Key Plastics, a U.S.-based manufacturer of plastic components and automotive parts.</p>
<p>Based in Belme in southern Normandy, Clearplas France manufactures plastic injection components for the automotive industry.</p>
<p>The total consideration would be payable in 6.7 million stg in cash and repayment of intra-group indebtedness of 1.9 million stg.</p>
<p>The proceeds will be used to reduce the group's bank borrowings.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
